tion "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x & =\\pi (\\frac{1}{2}+2n) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}+2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181784/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection/71961a7686019d9c14d583fcb0dca3f147837d52726a609159cb54549965847e" :answer/id #uuid "dfa3c2ae-01e9-52ad-b40e-6329a9c8d132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "de488b30-d34f-51e7-a97d-e3256c424287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "7555f3bb-db32-5a4d-9484-ec2151a98145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection/07bc5c10ee35ad58c7d8dd0d64cf41c03f03e5db34a2c66676cf702814ec0409" :answer/id #uuid "2ea75d78-3080-5e68-a933-428927c67284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection/a2883ba19b4b81bfe5f07fdc87d43374c3ef88b5b9a760fdfc647b8ab5307e88" :answer/id #uuid "eb7dd0dd-c4bb-5d7a-bbdc-e8dc12cf585d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a23e8b6c-9737-5db8-9eb4-88736f76a77a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181786/selection/71961a7686019d9c14d583fcb0dca3f147837d52726a609159cb54549965847e" :answer-field/choices ["q-181786/selection/71961a7686019d9c14d583fcb0dca3f147837d52726a609159cb54549965847e" "q-181786/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" "q-181786/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" "q-181786/selection/07bc5c10ee35ad58c7d8dd0d64cf41c03f03e5db34a2c66676cf702814ec0409" "q-181786/selection/a2883ba19b4b81bfe5f07fdc87d43374c3ef88b5b9a760fdfc647b8ab5307e88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181786" :question/id #uuid "f3e31501-59b7-5807-a5bb-b8096c3b5c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181786" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=-1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=-1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181786/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181786"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181143"] :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n \\\\ x & =\\frac{n}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181185"] :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\,\\pm 3\\pi ,\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\pm 3\\pi ,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13143"] :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $5n - 2 \\leq 21.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13176"] :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0.$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3 \\\\ -3<x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{ 0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13178"] :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: |k-1| \\leq 4 \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $|k-1| \\leq 4.$ So, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|k-1|\\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le k-1\\le 4 \\\\ -3\\le k\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13179"] :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{ x\\in \\mathbb R \\: :\\:  \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0  \\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
